  "summary": "Four candidates directly apply boosted decision-tree ensembles (gradient boosted trees) to predicting road traffic flow. [V0232] (Haddad et al., 2024) is a deployment study on LedgerGuard reporting MAE = 0.92. [V0231] (Gupta et al., 2023) evaluates on AgriSat-4 with accuracy 0.85. [V0230] (Fischer et al., 2022) applies the method to Atlas-ICU with test F1 of 0.78. [V0229] (El-Sayed et al., 2021) uses MetroFlow and reports AUROC 0.71. Because the reported metrics are heterogeneous (MAE, accuracy, F1, AUROC), the numbers are not directly comparable across studies, so the directly relevant four are ranked by recency. Only these four documents apply the requested method to the requested topic; the required fifth slot is filled by [V0208] (Gupta et al., 2023), which applies boosted decision-tree ensembles to predicting customer attrition (AgriSat-4, accuracy 0.75) — a method match but not a topic match, and therefore not directly relevant. Documents such as [V0092], [V0010], [V0022], [V0021], and [V0020] mention boosted decision trees for traffic flow only as prior work and are excluded, as are traffic-flow studies using other methods ([V0225], [V0222], [V0226], [V0234]) and boosted-tree studies on unrelated topics ([V0086], [V0136], [V0112]).",
